  <section class="sec" id="faq" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> FAQ</span>
        <h2>Hiring model questions, answered.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>What is the difference between nearshore and offshore? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">Distance and time zone overlap. Nearshore means a nearby country sharing most of your working hours, for US businesses typically Latin America. Offshore means a distant region such as Asia, with an 8 to 12 hour difference, lower rates, and collaboration that runs on shifted hours or asynchronously.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Can offshore employees work US hours? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">Yes. Offshore professionals routinely work US business hours, including overnight shifts in their own time zone. Remote Team Partners professionals work your schedule regardless of region, so overlap is a design choice, not a geographic limit.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Which model is cheapest? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">Offshore has the lowest rates, typically 50 to 70 percent below a comparable US hire's loaded cost. Nearshore runs 40 to 60 percent below. The cheapest model is not always the cheapest outcome: roles needing constant live collaboration can lose more to friction than they save on rates.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Which model is best for customer support? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">For support during US business hours, nearshore and shifted-hours offshore both work well. The Philippines is a long-established support hub with strong English. What matters most is dedicated staffing, training on your products, and QA, which our customer support service builds in.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Can I mix models across my team? <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">Yes, and most growing businesses do. Leadership and presence-based roles stay onshore, collaborative roles go nearshore, and process-driven operations go offshore, all managed as one team.</div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

